      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "**From top to bottom**, the points of intersection of the parabola ${y}^{2}-12x-2y-8=0$ with the $y$-axis are $A$ and $B.$ Find the coordinates of $A$ and $B.$\n\n$A(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)\\,$ and $\\,B(${{field-3}}$,$\n{{field-4}}$)$",
      "worked_solution": "When the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we set $x=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-12(0)-2y-8 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-2y-8 & =0 \\\\ (y+2)(y-4) & =0 \\\\ y & =-2,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the intersection points, from top to bottom, are $(0,4)$ and $(0,-2).$",
